{"kind":"report","text":"The W1 checkpoint is suitable for bounded client source preparation once its scheduling and attempt-lifecycle promises are made precise. This is feedback only, not implementation approval.\n\nThe complete public report is /tmp/artroom-w1-api-checkpoint.md, 9,800 bytes, SHA256 eecffbe98fff3eeb17248238d703fbe0e4b6713599e7a482351072027b31d4ef, at native baseline25467. Feedback request83dc69b3167e3dddc498c0c8064a80633a468ce5 / promisebe315e2c84edba71ef32838aed2715eaaa5bc99a leaves originald3f/c6a and full578/4073 open. Owner8edd already permits bounded source/cheap Node/types, with native selection required before Worker execution.\n\nThree lifecycle requirements should be explicit before source is frozen:\n\n1. Bound work during nonempty traffic too. A 1,024-byte frame limit bounds decoding, but yielding only for empty chunks does not bound a pump receiving immediately resolved valid heads or a huge concatenated chunk. Limit bytes/frames processed per task turn, yield to the task queue under all sustained traffic, and bound accepted raw chunks and helper-retained buffers. Coalesce notice state. Long sessions do not need a lifetime byte quota; the helper cannot promise to prevent allocations made by a noncompliant upstream.\n\n2. Invalidate and abort the attempt on EOF/error before a pending snapshot can emit current. Recheck its captured generation/context after awaits and before state changes or emission; old notices cannot update a newer attempt. A snapshot obtained after its subscription dies is retained/stale or reconnecting, rather than current. Keep refresh single-flight with one dirty reread. Preserve rendered-head monotonicity, reject same-sequence/different-hash conflicts and validate older notices before ignoring them.\n\n3. Dispose of late-opened bodies. Race ignoring open/read/snapshot callbacks against abort so local cancel/done resolves. If an abandoned open/fetch later returns a body, cancel/dispose it best-effort instead of merely discarding the result. Handle late rejections and prevent late repaint/reconnect. Local completion must not await an unresponsive physical cancel/native release. Exactly-once local cancellation is distinct from upstream compliance.\n\nThe subscribe-first design uses a sound existing seam: native Streams inserts its subscription before the first asynchronous pull, sends only head notices, checks summary permission before each new send, and holds one unread line while coalescing later heads. The Worker relay owns once-only release on EOF/failure/cancel. Current object first-call recovery can resume recorded work; this is not a global claim that stream opening has no other serving effects. A first validated notice followed by an authenticated complete snapshot can support the proposed local handoff. It does not prove missed-history replay, a room-wide atomic snapshot or command settlement.\n\nMake the public types concrete. Native Read\u003cT\u003e carries at/value/complete/optional next; Summary contains scope/definition, but has no at. T=Summary therefore needs an explicit local wrapper constructed from Read\u003cSummary\u003e, or a cleaner Read\u003cSummary\u003e entry API. The generic adapter must validate its own value and bounded same-head completeness; those are not new server proofs. Incomplete or cursor-bearing reads cannot become complete by relabeling. Existing Fetch has no headers, so a MIME check would need an explicit supported seam, not an invented property. Binding/MCP streaming remains unsupported unless its actual adapter supplies it.\n\nCopy/freeze the captured origin/full scope/incarnation/definition/membership/member/key. Native SessionClaims also names deployment: add an expected deployment or trusted origin-to-deployment binding, or disclose that this aspect is enforced by the server rather than checked by the helper. No current token bypass was found. A context or pin change cancels; reconnect cannot silently move an old view to another incarnation. Tokens and keys remain outside URLs, public states, reasons and logs.\n\nKeep bounded authentication/header/first-head waiting and renewal arithmetic explicit. Session.endedBy takes a native Timestamp, not the proposed numeric now callback directly. Local time triggers renewal; server clocks and authority decide access. EOF means disconnected, not proof of expiry/revocation. Actual forbidden/unauthorized renewal stops denial polling; expiry/clock-behind cannot authorize cached state. Reconnect obtains a new matching session, first validated head and complete current snapshot, with no Join/found/resign/command resend. Under hot traffic, follow owner8edd: emit valid obtained snapshots as explicitly retained/stale so updates do not hide every useful view, while never asserting they are current.\n\nFocused cheap witnesses should distinguish nonempty flood fairness, notice during snapshot, EOF during snapshot, cancel with ignoring callbacks, late body disposal, context/deployment/pin changes, raw-frame rejection before decode, renewed sessions and terminal denial. Existing native witness outcomes stay producer-attributed here; actual-route extension is needed only for a demonstrated new gap. No Node, native tests or gate were executed by checker.\n\nRoot and an independent reader freshly read the report through EOF; Root FULL-read peer seald7d7fb3 and owner8edd. Fresh254 native Read/Summary/Session/Streams/relay source corroborates these boundaries. The combined F1/W1 read/seal/native audit passed separately with exit0, SHA256848b6a59bc7cceef557b21931966d0295521d33bb4fdc7338c61b9b13887b9dc. Dependencies remain partial; no whole-native or prior9d7 transfer. Original Source/gate/review/hosted/access/custody duties remain. No new live backend, transport ABI, private probe or deployment is adopted.","body":{"audit_sha256":"848b6a59bc7cceef557b21931966d0295521d33bb4fdc7338c61b9b13887b9dc","checkpoint_sha256":"eecffbe98fff3eeb17248238d703fbe0e4b6713599e7a482351072027b31d4ef","metadata_verdict":"supported-with-required-contract-precision-before-frozen-source","promise":"be315e2c84edba71ef32838aed2715eaaa5bc99a"}}